# Vercel Web Analytics Integration

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Hono server project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` using pnpm (the project's package manager)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `pnpm-lock.yaml` with dependency resolution

### 2. Analytics Integration (index.ts)
- Added a new root endpoint (`GET /`) that serves an HTML page with Vercel Web Analytics
- Implemented analytics using the `inject()` function from `@vercel/analytics` via CDN
- The analytics script loads from `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@vercel/analytics@2.0.1/dist/index.js`
- Created a demo page that displays all available endpoints and confirms analytics are active

### 3. Code Quality
- Removed unused `Resource` import to fix linting errors
- Fixed code formatting issues (prettier)
- All linting checks pass successfully
- Preserved all existing functionality and endpoints

## Implementation Notes

### Why This Approach?
According to the official Vercel documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart and https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/package), Vercel Web Analytics is a **client-side analytics solution** designed for frontend applications. It supports:
- Next.js, React, Vue, Remix, Nuxt, SvelteKit, Astro
- Vanilla HTML/JavaScript via the `inject()` function

Since this is a **Hono backend API server**, there was no existing HTML serving capability. The documentation showed that Hono on Vercel can serve static files and HTML content, so I added a root endpoint that demonstrates proper analytics integration.

### What Gets Tracked?
When deployed to Vercel, the analytics will track:
- Page views on the root endpoint
- Visitor demographics (location, browser, OS)
- User engagement metrics
- Custom events (if added in the future)

### Framework-Specific Details
- Hono is not explicitly mentioned in the Vercel Analytics quickstart guide
- The vanilla JavaScript `inject()` approach is the appropriate method for this use case
- Analytics will only function when the app is deployed to Vercel (local development shows console logs)

## Files Modified

1. **e2e/servers/hono/package.json** - Added `@vercel/analytics` dependency
2. **e2e/servers/hono/index.ts** - Added root endpoint with analytics integration and cleaned up imports
3. **pnpm-lock.yaml** - Updated with new dependency tree

## Preserved Functionality

All existing endpoints remain fully functional:
- `GET /protected` - Payment-protected endpoint
- `GET /health` - Health check
- `POST /close` - Graceful shutdown
- `GET /` - **NEW**: Analytics demo page

## Next Steps

When deploying to Vercel:
1. The analytics will automatically start tracking page views
2. View analytics in the Vercel dashboard under your project's Analytics tab
3. No additional configuration is needed on Vercel's side
4. Custom events can be tracked by importing `track()` from `@vercel/analytics` if needed

